  "instructions": [
    {
      "primary_message": "Preheat oven to 375°F.\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Using a serrated or bread knife, cut the baguette crosswise into 6 portions. Holding the knife parallel to the cutting board, cut each portion in half horizontally, separating it into 2 pieces, top and bottom. (You should have 12 pieces total.)",
      "secondary_message": "1 loaf baguette"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Arrange baguette pieces on a large baking sheet pan, cut-side facing up.",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "To assemble the pizzas, spread pizza sauce over half of the baguette pieces and basil pesto over the other half of the pieces. Sprinkle with cheese, Italian seasoning, and salt.",
      "secondary_message": "½ (14 oz) jar pizza sauce\n½ cup basil pesto\n1 ½ cups shredded cheese, Italian blend\n½ tsp Italian seasoning\n⅛ tsp salt"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Place pizzas in the oven and bake for 5 minutes, until the cheese just starts to melt down and set. Remove from oven and set aside to cool slightly.",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Meanwhile, count out 24 olives, one olive for each spider (reserve remaining olives for another use). Cut olives in half lengthwise. Set 24 halves aside (these will be the spider bodies); cut the remaining 24 olive halves lengthwise into 6 thin strips (these will be the legs).",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Top the pizzas with olives, arranging them in the design of a spider. (You will need 1 olive half plus 6 olive legs per spider.)\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Return pizzas to the oven and continue to bake until the baguette is crispy and cheese is melted, 5 minutes more. Remove from oven.",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Transfer pizzas to a serving platter and enjoy warm!",
      "secondary_message": null
    }
  ],
